ype":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" state is a map of column IDs to boolean values. A column will be hidden if its ID is present in the map and the value is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":". If the column ID is not present in the map, or the value is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":", the column will be shown."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you need to own the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" state yourself (for example, to persist user preferences), the recommended v9 approach is an external atom (created with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAtom"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-store"},{"type":"text","value":") passed to the table's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"atoms"},{"type":"text","value":" option. External atoms give you fine-grained subscriptions anywhere in your app, and other code can read or write the visibility state without re-running the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"injectTable"},{"type":"text","value":" options initializer on every change."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createAtom } from '@tanstack/angular-store'\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport type { ColumnVisibilityState } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly columnVisibilityAtom = createAtom<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n    columnId1: true,\n    columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n    columnId3: true,\n  })\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    //...\n    atoms: {\n      columnVisibility: this.columnVisibilityAtom,\n    },\n  }))\n\n  // read this.columnVisibilityAtom.get() wherever you need the value\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, the v8-style "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state.columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" plus "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onColumnVisibilityChange"},{"type":"text","value":" pattern is still supported. In Angular this means owning the slice with an Angular signal. It can be convenient for simple integrations or when migrating v8 code, but it is less fine-grained than external atoms. See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./table-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Table State Guide"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for a deeper comparison."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nreadonly columnVisibility = signal<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n  columnId1: true,\n  columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n  columnId3: true,\n})\n\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  //...\n  state: {\n    columnVisibility: this.columnVisibility(),\n    //...\n  },\n  onColumnVisibilityChange: (updater) =>\n    typeof updater === 'function'\n      ? this.columnVisibility.update(updater)\n      : this.columnVisibility.set(updater),\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Alternatively, if you don't need to manage the column visibility state outside of the table, you can still set the initial default column visibility state using the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" option."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" is provided to both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":", the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" initialization will take precedence and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" will be ignored. Do not provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"columnVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" to both "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialState"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":", only one or the other."}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  //...\n  initialState: {\n    columnVisibility: {\n      columnId1: true,\n      columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n      columnId3: true,\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n}))","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"disable-hiding-columns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disable Hiding Columns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, all columns can be hidden or shown. If you want to prevent certain columns from being hidden, you set the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableHiding"},{"type":"text","value":" column option to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":" for those columns."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const columns = [\n  {\n    header: 'ID',\n    accessorKey: 'id',\n    enableHiding: false, // disable hiding for this column\n  },\n  {\n    header: 'Name',\n    accessorKey: 'name', // can be hidden\n  },\n]","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-visibility-toggle-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility Toggle APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are several column API methods that are useful for rendering column visibility toggles in the UI."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getCanHide"},{"type":"text","value":" - Useful for disabling the visibility toggle for a column that has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"enableHiding"},{"type":"text","value":" set to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getIsVisible"},{"type":"text","value":" - Useful for setting the initial state of the visibility toggle."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.toggleVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" - Useful for toggling the visibility of a column."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler"},{"type":"text","value":" - Shortcut for hooking up the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"column.toggleVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" method to a UI event handler."}]}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"@for (column of table.getAllLeafColumns(); track column.id) {\n<label>\n  <input\n    type=\"checkbox\"\n    [checked]=\"column.getIsVisible()\"\n    [disabled]=\"!column.getCanHide()\"\n    (change)=\"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler()?.($event)\"\n  />\n  {{ column.id }}\n</label>\n}","lang":"html"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"column-visibility-aware-table-apis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Column Visibility Aware Table APIs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When you render your header, body, and footer cells, there are a lot of API options available. You may see APIs like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getAllLeafColumns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getAllCells"},{"type":"text","value":", but if you use these APIs, they will not take column visibility into account. Instead, you need to use the \"visible\" variants of these APIs, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"table.getVisibleLeafColumns"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"row.getVisibleCells"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      @for (column of table.getVisibleLeafColumns(); track column.id) {\n      <th>{{ column.id }}</th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\"\n          >{{ renderCell }}</ng-container\n        >\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using the Header Group APIs, they will already take column visibility into account."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"column-visibility-setup","text":"Column Visibility Setup","level":3},{"id":"column-visibility-angular-guide","text":"Column Visibility (Angular) Guide","level":2},{"id":"column-visibility-state","text":"Column Visibility State","level":3},{"id":"disable-hiding-columns","text":"Disable Hiding Columns","level":3},{"id":"column-visibility-toggle-apis","text":"Column Visibility Toggle APIs","level":3},{"id":"column-visibility-aware-table-apis","text":"Column Visibility Aware Table APIs","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these Angular examples:\n\n- [Column Visibility](../examples/column-visibility)\n\n### Column Visibility Setup\n\nHere's how you set up your table to use column visibility features. Adding the column visibility feature enables the related APIs.\n\n```ts\nimport { signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly data = signal(defaultData)\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n## Column Visibility (Angular) Guide\n\nThe column visibility feature allows table columns to be hidden or shown dynamically. In v9, add `columnVisibilityFeature` to your `features` to enable this. There is a dedicated `columnVisibility` state and APIs for managing column visibility dynamically.\n\n### Column Visibility State\n\nThe `columnVisibility` state is a map of column IDs to boolean values. A column will be hidden if its ID is present in the map and the value is `false`. If the column ID is not present in the map, or the value is `true`, the column will be shown.\n\nIf you need to own the `columnVisibility` state yourself (for example, to persist user preferences), the recommended v9 approach is an external atom (created with `createAtom` from `@tanstack/angular-store`) passed to the table's `atoms` option. External atoms give you fine-grained subscriptions anywhere in your app, and other code can read or write the visibility state without re-running the `injectTable` options initializer on every change.\n\n```ts\nimport { createAtom } from '@tanstack/angular-store'\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport type { ColumnVisibilityState } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly columnVisibilityAtom = createAtom<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n    columnId1: true,\n    columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n    columnId3: true,\n  })\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    //...\n    atoms: {\n      columnVisibility: this.columnVisibilityAtom,\n    },\n  }))\n\n  // read this.columnVisibilityAtom.get() wherever you need the value\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, the v8-style `state.columnVisibility` plus `onColumnVisibilityChange` pattern is still supported. In Angular this means owning the slice with an Angular signal. It can be convenient for simple integrations or when migrating v8 code, but it is less fine-grained than external atoms. See the [Table State Guide](./table-state) for a deeper comparison.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nreadonly columnVisibility = signal<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n  columnId1: true,\n  columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n  columnId3: true,\n})\n\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  //...\n  state: {\n    columnVisibility: this.columnVisibility(),\n    //...\n  },\n  onColumnVisibilityChange: (updater) =>\n    typeof updater === 'function'\n      ? this.columnVisibility.update(updater)\n      : this.columnVisibility.set(updater),\n}))\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you don't need to manage the column visibility state outside of the table, you can still set the initial default column visibility state using the `initialState` option.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> If `columnVisibility` is provided to both `initialState` and `state`, the `state` initialization will take precedence and `initialState` will be ignored. Do not provide `columnVisibility` to both `initialState` and `state`, only one or the other.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  //...\n  initialState: {\n    columnVisibility: {\n      columnId1: true,\n      columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n      columnId3: true,\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n### Disable Hiding Columns\n\nBy default, all columns can be hidden or shown. If you want to prevent certain columns from being hidden, you set the `enableHiding` column option to `false` for those columns.\n\n```ts\nconst columns = [\n  {\n    header: 'ID',\n    accessorKey: 'id',\n    enableHiding: false, // disable hiding for this column\n  },\n  {\n    header: 'Name',\n    accessorKey: 'name', // can be hidden\n  },\n]\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Toggle APIs\n\nThere are several column API methods that are useful for rendering column visibility toggles in the UI.\n\n- `column.getCanHide` - Useful for disabling the visibility toggle for a column that has `enableHiding` set to `false`.\n- `column.getIsVisible` - Useful for setting the initial state of the visibility toggle.\n- `column.toggleVisibility` - Useful for toggling the visibility of a column.\n- `column.getToggleVisibilityHandler` - Shortcut for hooking up the `column.toggleVisibility` method to a UI event handler.\n\n```html\n@for (column of table.getAllLeafColumns(); track column.id) {\n<label>\n  <input\n    type=\"checkbox\"\n    [checked]=\"column.getIsVisible()\"\n    [disabled]=\"!column.getCanHide()\"\n    (change)=\"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler()?.($event)\"\n  />\n  {{ column.id }}\n</label>\n}\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Aware Table APIs\n\nWhen you render your header, body, and footer cells, there are a lot of API options available. You may see APIs like `table.getAllLeafColumns` and `row.getAllCells`, but if you use these APIs, they will not take column visibility into account. Instead, you need to use the \"visible\" variants of these APIs, such as `table.getVisibleLeafColumns` and `row.getVisibleCells`.\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      @for (column of table.getVisibleLeafColumns(); track column.id) {\n      <th>{{ column.id }}</th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\"\n          >{{ renderCell }}</ng-container\n        >\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\nIf you are using the Header Group APIs, they will already take column visibility into account.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Column Visibility (Angular) Guide\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these Angular examples:\n\n- [Column Visibility](../examples/column-visibility)\n\n### Column Visibility Setup\n\nHere's how you set up your table to use column visibility features. Adding the column visibility feature enables the related APIs.\n\n```ts\nimport { signal } from '@angular/core'\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly data = signal(defaultData)\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    columns,\n    data: this.data(),\n  }))\n}\n```\n\n## Column Visibility (Angular) Guide\n\nThe column visibility feature allows table columns to be hidden or shown dynamically. In v9, add `columnVisibilityFeature` to your `features` to enable this. There is a dedicated `columnVisibility` state and APIs for managing column visibility dynamically.\n\n### Column Visibility State\n\nThe `columnVisibility` state is a map of column IDs to boolean values. A column will be hidden if its ID is present in the map and the value is `false`. If the column ID is not present in the map, or the value is `true`, the column will be shown.\n\nIf you need to own the `columnVisibility` state yourself (for example, to persist user preferences), the recommended v9 approach is an external atom (created with `createAtom` from `@tanstack/angular-store`) passed to the table's `atoms` option. External atoms give you fine-grained subscriptions anywhere in your app, and other code can read or write the visibility state without re-running the `injectTable` options initializer on every change.\n\n```ts\nimport { createAtom } from '@tanstack/angular-store'\nimport {\n  injectTable,\n  tableFeatures,\n  columnVisibilityFeature,\n} from '@tanstack/angular-table'\nimport type { ColumnVisibilityState } from '@tanstack/angular-table'\n\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nexport class App {\n  readonly columnVisibilityAtom = createAtom<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n    columnId1: true,\n    columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n    columnId3: true,\n  })\n\n  readonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n    features,\n    //...\n    atoms: {\n      columnVisibility: this.columnVisibilityAtom,\n    },\n  }))\n\n  // read this.columnVisibilityAtom.get() wherever you need the value\n}\n```\n\nAlternatively, the v8-style `state.columnVisibility` plus `onColumnVisibilityChange` pattern is still supported. In Angular this means owning the slice with an Angular signal. It can be convenient for simple integrations or when migrating v8 code, but it is less fine-grained than external atoms. See the [Table State Guide](./table-state) for a deeper comparison.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nreadonly columnVisibility = signal<ColumnVisibilityState>({\n  columnId1: true,\n  columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n  columnId3: true,\n})\n\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  //...\n  state: {\n    columnVisibility: this.columnVisibility(),\n    //...\n  },\n  onColumnVisibilityChange: (updater) =>\n    typeof updater === 'function'\n      ? this.columnVisibility.update(updater)\n      : this.columnVisibility.set(updater),\n}))\n```\n\nAlternatively, if you don't need to manage the column visibility state outside of the table, you can still set the initial default column visibility state using the `initialState` option.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> If `columnVisibility` is provided to both `initialState` and `state`, the `state` initialization will take precedence and `initialState` will be ignored. Do not provide `columnVisibility` to both `initialState` and `state`, only one or the other.\n\n```ts\nconst features = tableFeatures({ columnVisibilityFeature })\n\nreadonly table = injectTable(() => ({\n  features,\n  //...\n  initialState: {\n    columnVisibility: {\n      columnId1: true,\n      columnId2: false, // hide this column by default\n      columnId3: true,\n    },\n    //...\n  },\n}))\n```\n\n### Disable Hiding Columns\n\nBy default, all columns can be hidden or shown. If you want to prevent certain columns from being hidden, you set the `enableHiding` column option to `false` for those columns.\n\n```ts\nconst columns = [\n  {\n    header: 'ID',\n    accessorKey: 'id',\n    enableHiding: false, // disable hiding for this column\n  },\n  {\n    header: 'Name',\n    accessorKey: 'name', // can be hidden\n  },\n]\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Toggle APIs\n\nThere are several column API methods that are useful for rendering column visibility toggles in the UI.\n\n- `column.getCanHide` - Useful for disabling the visibility toggle for a column that has `enableHiding` set to `false`.\n- `column.getIsVisible` - Useful for setting the initial state of the visibility toggle.\n- `column.toggleVisibility` - Useful for toggling the visibility of a column.\n- `column.getToggleVisibilityHandler` - Shortcut for hooking up the `column.toggleVisibility` method to a UI event handler.\n\n```html\n@for (column of table.getAllLeafColumns(); track column.id) {\n<label>\n  <input\n    type=\"checkbox\"\n    [checked]=\"column.getIsVisible()\"\n    [disabled]=\"!column.getCanHide()\"\n    (change)=\"column.getToggleVisibilityHandler()?.($event)\"\n  />\n  {{ column.id }}\n</label>\n}\n```\n\n### Column Visibility Aware Table APIs\n\nWhen you render your header, body, and footer cells, there are a lot of API options available. You may see APIs like `table.getAllLeafColumns` and `row.getAllCells`, but if you use these APIs, they will not take column visibility into account. Instead, you need to use the \"visible\" variants of these APIs, such as `table.getVisibleLeafColumns` and `row.getVisibleCells`.\n\n```html\n<table>\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      @for (column of table.getVisibleLeafColumns(); track column.id) {\n      <th>{{ column.id }}</th>\n      }\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    @for (row of table.getRowModel().rows; track row.id) {\n    <tr>\n      @for (cell of row.getVisibleCells(); track cell.id) {\n      <td>\n        <ng-container *flexRenderCell=\"cell; let renderCell\"\n          >{{ renderCell }}</ng-container\n        >\n      </td>\n      }\n    </tr>\n    }\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n```\n\nIf you are using the Header Group APIs, they will already take column visibility into account.\n"}
